Patch 43. In the series since 2026-10-17, after patch 42.

ReXApp (src/ui/rex_app.cpp) puts its config, <app>.toml (which the settings dialog saves), and
its logs next to the executable. On Android the executable's folder is the app's native library
folder, read-only or inside the APK, so neither could be written. There they go with the user
data (user_data_root, by default the user folder, which the Android main points at the app's
internal storage), or with user_data_root where the app's OnConfigurePaths moved it, and that
folder is made then (on a fresh install nothing else has made it when the settings are first
saved). An app can still move both (OnConfigurePaths, OnConfigureLogging). Every other platform
is unchanged.

Test: built for Android and Linux here, and for Windows and macOS by CI. On the POCO X7 the game
runs with no write error; its settings and logs are where the game's own ConfigurePaths puts them
(src/live/install.cpp), so this patch's defaults are not what placed them: they matter to
apps that keep the defaults.

